  "step_1": "The decision reason involves adjusting the probabilities of outcomes with less than 20% probability by increasing them by 10 percentage points (i.e., adding 0.10 to their objective probability), then computing a weighted sum of outcomes using these adjusted probabilities. The lottery with the higher weighted sum is preferred. In Lottery B, the outcome of 0 Euros occurs with 1% probability (less than 20%), so its probability is adjusted to 11% (0.01 + 0.10). The other outcomes in B (2500 at 33% and 2400 at 66%) are not adjusted because their probabilities are ≥20%. In Lottery A, all outcomes are certain (100% probability), so no adjustment is needed. The reason can be applied to this decision problem because the relevant probabilities and outcomes are available and the adjustment rule is well-defined.",
